# SmartSwap AI — Cursor Project Rules

You are an expert full-stack engineer and software architect working on SmartSwap AI.
Strictly adhere to the following non-negotiable guidelines:

## 1. Graph-First Token Discipline
- ALWAYS read `docs/graph/CODE_MAP.md` FIRST before scanning or reading repository files.
- NEVER scan `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `build/`, `android/app/build/`, or unrelated modules.
- Only load files inside your assigned domain boundary.
- If endpoints, services, or models change, run `npm run graphify` to sync the dependency graph.

## 2. Localization & Theme Defaults
- Default locale: Spanish (`es`). English (`en`) is an optional user toggle (`smartswap_locale`).
- Default theme: Light mode (`light`). Dark mode (`dark`) is an optional user toggle (`smartswap_theme`).
- Brand Colors:
  - Primary: `#00685f` (Teal)
  - Secondary / Accent: `#fd761a` (Orange)

## 3. Architecture & Code Boundaries
- Strict TypeScript: No implicit `any`, zero `any` usage. All DTOs validated with Zod.
- Backend (`api/`):
  - Architecture: `Controllers` (`@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)`) -> `Services` (Prisma `$transaction`) -> `Mappers`.
  - Security: NEVER expose `passwordHash`. NEVER accept unvalidated body payloads.
- Frontend (`mobile/`):
  - NEVER call `fetch()` directly inside React components or UI hooks.
  - All network traffic goes through `src/services/http/apiClient.ts` via structured service layers (`services/auth`, `services/items`, `services/routes`, `services/ai`).
  - NEVER put `OPENAI_API_KEY` or `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` in mobile code or `.env`.

## 4. Git Standards
- Conventional Commits: `<type>(<scope>): <description>` (e.g., `feat(routes): ...`, `fix(auth): ...`).
- Atomic commits with a single responsibility.
- Verify working tree cleanliness with `git status` before finishing.

## 5. Verification Commands
- `npm run graphify`: Update code map and dependency graph.
- `npm run typecheck`: Verify TypeScript compilation across monorepo.
- `npm run test:api` / `npm run test:mobile`: Verify test suites.
